Multichar_Symbols
  +N    ! noun
  +A    ! adjective
  +Pron ! pronoun
  +Num  ! numeral
  +V    ! verb
  +Adv  ! adverb
  +Pr   ! preposition
  +Adp  ! adposition (umbrella; +Po für Postposition)
  +Po   ! postposition (Twanksta desc "psp"; paggan — governs preceding genitive)
  +CC   ! coordinating conjunction
  +CS   ! subordinating conjunction
  +Pcle ! particle
  +Interj ! interjection
  +Prop ! proper-noun sub-POS (N+Prop — Eigenname, Orts-/Personenname)

  +Sg   ! singular
  +Pl   ! plural

  +Nom  ! nominative
  +Gen  ! genitive
  +Dat  ! dative
  +Acc  ! accusative

  +Msc  ! masculine
  +Fem  ! feminine
  +Neu  ! neuter

  +Prs  ! present tense
  +Prt  ! preterite tense
  +Inf  ! infinitive
  +Ind  ! indicative mood
  +Opt  ! optative
  +Imprt ! imperative
  +Subj ! subjunctive
  +Rel  ! modus relativus (hearsay; only corpus-attested forms, e.g. astits)
  +Refl ! reflexive (si-verb)

  ! Finite Person/Numerus fusioniert (Giella-Stil): sg1/sg2/sp3/pl1/pl2.
  ! Die 3. Person ist im Apreußischen numeruslos (3sg = 3pl, Twanksta
  ! 3828/3828 identisch), darum +SP3 ohne Sg/Pl.
  +Sg1  +Sg2  +SP3  +Pl1  +Pl2

  ! Partizipien: TYP (PrsPrc/PrfPrc) + Voice (Act/Pss) + Genus/Numerus/Kasus.
  +PrsPrc +PrfPrc +Act +Pss

  +Comp ! comparative degree
  +Superl ! superlative degree
  +Card ! cardinal numeral (one, two, three…)
  +Ord  ! ordinal numeral (first, second, third…)
  +Encl ! enclitic pronoun (di, dis, din — proclitic subject replacement)

  ! Morphophonology trigger: deaccent (mobile stem under a strong participle
  ! ending). Sits on the surface tape at the stem|ending boundary; stress.twolc
  ! shortens the preceding long stem vowel / degeminates, then deletes it.
  DEAC

  ! Flag diacritics for divergence layers
  @P.standard.prusaspira@
  @P.standard.twanksta@
  @P.verb_theme.i@
  @P.verb_theme.a@
  @P.iotation.surface@
  @P.iotation.leveled@
